---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Header from '../components/Header.astro'; import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'; import Icons from '../components/Icons.astro';
const stages=[['01','Inspection','Defined checks support careful review at relevant stages.'],['02','Hygiene & handling','Clean handling practices help protect product integrity.'],['03','Traceability','Batch information can help make supply conversations clearer.'],['04','Dispatch review','A final review supports careful coordination through the supply channel.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Technology & Quality | DFL Eggs"><Header /><main><section class="page-hero teal"><div class="wrap narrow"><p class="eyebrow light-eyebrow">Technology & Quality</p><h1>Precision with a clear purpose: <em>healthier starts.</em></h1><p>Technology helps make key DFL processes more consistent and measurable. It complements—not replaces—careful human oversight and sound sericulture practice.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap split-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p><h2>More consistency in a process often shaped by <em>seasonal variation.</em></h2></div><div><p>High manual involvement can introduce variation when teams, timings and conditions change. DFL Eggs is intended to reduce avoidable process dependence through technology-supported checks and repeatable handling steps.</p></div></div></section><section class="section tech-stages"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Quality control stages</p><div class="stage-grid">{stages.map(([num,title,text])=><article><span>{num}</span><Icons name="quality"/><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section><section class="section proof"><div class="wrap proof-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">About the accuracy claim</p><h2>Numbers need context <em>before confidence.</em></h2><p>“98.6% accuracy” must not be used as a standalone claim. Before publishing, define exactly what is being measured, the method and benchmark used, the observation period, the sample size, and who validated the result.</p></div><aside><p class="mono">PENDING EVIDENCE</p><h3>Accuracy statement checklist</h3><ul class="check-list"><li>What decision or detection is measured?</li><li>Compared with which verified reference?</li><li>Under what operating conditions?</li><li>What independent evidence can be linked?</li></ul></aside></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap prose-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p><h2>Quality is a system, not a single <em>claim.</em></h2></div><div><p>Good quality practice can include disciplined hygiene, inspection, traceability, careful storage and handling, and honest communication about product availability. Certificates, lab reports or standard references should be displayed here only when they are current and approved for public use.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/#enquiry">Ask a quality question <span>→</span></a></div></div></section></main><Footer /></BaseLayout>
